SEL relays: ``protection_schemes`` in ``parsed-config.json`` now includes every enabled ``E<two-digit code>`` element setting whose value isn't ``N``, ``NO``, ``OFF``, ``NONE``, ``0`` or empty, also when the code isn't in ``ANSI_CODES`` (the SEL-710's ``E47T`` and ``E49MOTOR`` weren't found before) or the value is a mode such as ``AUTO``, ``C2`` or ``INT``, and a missing ``EVOLT`` setting no longer raises an error that was silently ignored. The duplicate keys and typos in ``ANSI_CODES`` are fixed: ``51``, ``27X`` and ``87S`` were "Overload", "Line Undervoltage" and "Percent Differential", and are now "AC Inverse Time Overcurrent Relay", "Auxiliary Undervoltage" and "Stator Differential".
